  "note": "Triennial election of the Dromore (Co. Down) Urban Council, polled Tuesday 15 January 1929. Seven candidates were nominated for the nine seats and the returning officer nominated two retiring members to fill the vacancies, so there was no contest (Belfast News-Letter, 8 January 1929, p. 10). Captain Hunter, town clerk and returning officer, nominated Messrs. Robert J. M'Fadden and E. Boal, two of the retiring members, to fill the vacancies. Returned unopposed."
